        '3-5', $q$Tiny Fliers$q$, $q$(1) Hummingbirds are some of the smallest birds in the world. (2) Many of them weigh less than a nickel. (3) Even though they are tiny, they are amazing fliers.

(4) A hummingbird can move its wings very fast. (5) Some kinds beat their wings more than fifty times in one second. (6) This makes the humming sound that gives the bird its name. (7) Hummingbirds can hover in one spot like a helicopter. (8) They can even fly backward. (9) My aunt has a red bird feeder on her porch.

(10) Flying so fast uses a lot of energy. (11) Hummingbirds drink sweet nectar from flowers to get that energy. (12) They also eat tiny insects for protein. (13) A hummingbird may visit hundreds of flowers in a single day.$q$, 'draft')
