        '3-5', $q$The Art of Folding Paper$q$, $q$(1) Origami is the art of folding paper into shapes. (2) The word comes from Japan. (3) "Ori" means fold, and "kami" means paper.

(4) Origami artists usually start with one square sheet of paper. (5) They do not cut the paper or use glue. (6) Instead, they make careful folds, one after another. (7) A valley fold bends the paper toward you. (8) A mountain fold bends it away from you. (9) By mixing these folds, artists can make animals, flowers and boxes.

(10) One of the best-known origami shapes is the crane. (11) A crane is a tall bird with long legs. (12) Folding paper also helps people practice patience. (13) You have to follow each step in order. (14) My sister once folded a paper frog that could hop.$q$, 'draft')
